let's talk about Donald Trump's  commandeering of American television to  propagandize about the border wall over  which he shut down the government last  night  we will talk about the content of this  address I mentioned yesterday during a  live stream that I did covering this and  and also earlier on yesterday's show  that there are really kind of three  issues here number one is is there  actually an undocumented immigration  crisis I laid out the case yesterday for  why there is not secondly if there were  such an immigration crisis would the  wall that Donald Trump is proposing be  the solution to that crisis I explained  why it would not and then issue number  three layer number three was would a  presidential address of this type in  primetime on television  be the right place for overt political  lobbying for the policy that Donald  Trump wants and I also made the case  that it was not and the LA the the  speech in the end was nine minutes long  half just lies at a rate that we maybe  have not seen previously during a Trump  speech the other half just anecdotal  appeals to emotion and I'm not gonna  focus too too much on those because I  think our audience mostly understands  that you don't make policy based on  anecdotal appeals to emotion but we  should talk about the lies that we're  told because that actually is important  but the primary takeaway is this address  never should have happened it was purely  political it was a lobbying speech I  actually would be okay with a  presidential address in primetime on all  TV networks for lobbying the public  about a real emergency or a crisis right  we have a climate change emergency on  our planet if we had a president say I'm  going to address the American people  because of the crisis that is climate  change in what we're doing to our planet  that would actually make sense because  it's real a real crisis could be we've  got a president who's an accused serial  sex assault er with at least one child  accuser that is more of a crisis than  the crisis of undocumented immigrants  coming over the us-mexico border so  there are many ways in which I would  support a president saying I need to  address the nation tonight  this is not one of them and most of the  lies that Trump told were told up front  I'll go through a few of them I'm not  gonna play the nine minute thing because  it's only nine minutes and it's very  easy to find I'll focus just on  analyzing the lies that we're told  Donald Trump called this he sort of  opened this thing yesterday calling it a  growing crisis and as I've already  outlined it's not a crisis at all but  it's definitely not growing there's no  evidence that this is a growing problem  border crossings are lower and lower and  lower each year dating all the way back  to the year 2000 there has been an  increase in the last few months but  that's mostly asylum seekers who are  people going through the correct legal  process to ask for asylum in the United  States Donald Trump said we don't have  any way of returning people to where  they came from quickly quickly is  subjective but we do have a mechanism  for doing that however the fact that  Trump has shut down government is  actually what's slowing that process  down making it so that immigration  hearings have slowed down to an absolute  halt Trump arguing that we are really  hurt economically that this is a strain  on resources undocumented immigrants  that does not appear to be true  undocumented immigrants pay in to social  welfare programs from which they will  never get money back out they are  single-handedly holding on their backs  and shoulders multiple industries which  would collapse without them and most  importantly Donald Trump made the case  that economically undocumented  immigration is hurting the United States  because undocumented immigrants drive  wages down what is an amazing ruse about  that is that it's the corporation's  who want to pay lower wages that are the  ones benefiting from that and it's an  unbelievably a brazen act of misplaced  ire to be mad at the people coming here  to work for a better life than the  corporations that take advantage of them  and choose to hire undocumented  immigrants without being punished if we  started enforcing penalties on  corporations that hire undocumented  immigrants  you would solve an overwhelming majority  of the problem if corporations weren't  known to hire undocumented immigrants  then you wouldn't have so many people  getting jobs and looking for jobs it  would be a problem that in great part  would fix itself then Trump talked about  Americans are dying from drugs that are  coming over the us-mexico border listen  that that is it's true that Americans  are dying from drugs but that's not  coming exclusively because of drugs  coming over the us-mexico border a lot  of it is marijuana first of all which  nobody is dying from and secondly  according to the DEA it's mostly being  smuggled through ports of entry not  through the parts of the border which  would be blocked with Trump's border  wall ok understand that most of the  drugs coming into the United States from  Mexico are coming hidden and smuggled in  vehicles and on persons through the  actual legitimate on-the-record ports of  entry meaning a wall wouldn't do  anything about it Donald Trump is saying  that thousands of Americans are being  killed by undocumented immigrants yearly  I was not able to find data that  supports that although I'm open to  having my mind changed Trump insisting  that it's a humanitarian crisis well  just saying that doesn't actually make  it so and then Trump starting to move  into the appeal to emotion phase of his  address by saying women and children are  the biggest victims of undocumented  immigration that is true but women and  children are always the biggest victims  period all over the world from all sorts  of circumstances that doesn't justify a  wall between the u.s. and Mexico and it  doesn't prove that we have an  undocumented immigration crisis Donald  Trump deliberately conflated border  security and a 25 billion dollar wall or  35 billion dollar wall by the time it's  all said and done and what's really  important to understand there is that  it's untrue what Trump said that  Democrats aren't willing to fund border  security Democrats have actually been  willing to provide border security  funding not for the wall but for  technology and  Staffing in exchange for reopening  government and it's Mitch McConnell and  Donald Trump who have refused to give  any of those bills any serious  consideration it is untrue also that  everybody wanted a wall until Trump was  president and all of a sudden they don't  just because as a Democrat you might  have been willing years ago to give  Republicans some border fencing a few  miles of it in exchange for things you  wanted doesn't mean you're a hypocrite  because you now don't want a twenty five  thirty or thirty-five billion dollar  wall across the entire border so big  picture you have a government that is  not shut down because of Democrats Trump  shut it down you have a president who  has failed to get what he wants and is  now throwing a literal temper tantrum  which caused him to commandeer  television networks for nine minutes  plus the lead-up coverage and the Pelosi  Schumer follow-up speech and the  analysis of it for several hours across  multiple networks and most importantly  there is no crisis and at least for now  Pat there's no indication that this  address has really moved the needle for  Donald Trump  well we'll see I think this comes across  as effective propaganda honestly because  you have the president on his own turf  in the Oval Office delivering a speech  to the nation calling the immigration  situation of crisis calling it an  emergency I think that's going to be  effective about you know people just  tuning in to their local programming on  CBS or NBC wanting to watch their  favorite show they may not follow  politics that closely they may not stick  around and hear the fact checks here the  response is given by Pelosi closely and  Schumer and you know at this moment a  majority or at least a plurality of  Americans blame Trump for the shutdown I  would not be surprised if in the coming  days we see that that's flipped a little  bit those numbers may shift but you're  already starting to see even  conservative political analysts say it  looks like Trump is going to fail and  he's going to have to relent and allow  government to be reopened we will talk a  little bit more about that but in the  short term I don't see this helping  Donald Trump it came off is so not  credible it came off as so flaccid and  beta in every way  and it also may have been an illegal use  of government resources for Trump's  campaign because minutes before the  speech the reelect trump campaign sent  out an email asking for donations on the  basis of the immigration crisis and  previewing Trump's speech and if you  consider that sort of part of Trump's  campaign this was a political speech  used in this manner to help his campaign  and there are possible ways in that that  made have even violated campaign finance  law although I wouldn't expect him to be  held accountable for it we will follow  it and see what the impact is

